  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Joint, differentiable, and statistically defined density methods now address noisy cryo-EM and cryo-ET data across tasks from reconstruction to picking.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing sequential or manually tuned density-processing steps with integrated, differentiable, or statistically defined procedures that handle noisy data directly. End2EndPtychoSPA fits a 3D potential and particle poses jointly to 4D-STEM data through a differentiable multislice model rather than reconstructing sequentially. EB-FM learns flow-based priors over atomic structures from noisy cryo-EM projections via stochastic EM. Astex-Faro applies a reference-ensemble statistical framework, with a new FSCoh consistency metric, to flag significant density deviations in cryo-EM maps for drug discovery hit identification. RobPicker, a meta-learning framework, corrects label noise and reweights rare species to improve macromolecule picking in cryo-ET tomograms. The items address distinct tasks, so the thread is dominant rather than shared by every item, but the common element is computational statistical or learned treatment of noisy density data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-08"
}
